{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/396477-how-to-st-a-thread-for-new-players-and-storytellers","id":396477,"title":"How to ST: A thread for New Players and Storytellers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-07T10:40:14-08:00","id":396477,"title":"How to ST: A thread for New Players and Storytellers","content":"This ia thread made for give advice, tips in the general sense and to give some directions to the young generations that will take over our role once we &quot;Quit&quot;*<br /> Ill give my fair share of advices and as well i will sum up my vision of roleplaying games in a quote i always bear in my heart.<br /> I first started to roleplay when i was 12 or 13 years old , this was about 11 or 12 years ago.<br /> When i first went to my local roleplaying shop, i meet a lot of people from which i meet 3 great St and even greater friends that thought me how to ST. the main lesson they gave me was one<br /> &quot;To ST/DM/Gm, its to serve.&quot;<br /> <br /> After that , i elarn to respect your fellow DM. theres good players, bad players, great storytellers and some who lack the skill but carry the passion.<br /> So, remember...<br /> <br /> <i>..We few, we happy few, we band of brothers;<br /> For he to-day that sheds his Dices and Rolls with me<br /> Shall be my brother...</i><br /> <br /> -IF you can tell real life from the game, stop playing.<br /> -Investigate your players, i mean get to know them before you decide to run a game to them. i usually never ST to strangers, only to close friends.<br /> -Rules and Canon are meant to be Broken.<br /> -Have Fun<br /> -Read a Lot<br /> -The art of Improvisation is a double edge sword, be careful with this.<br /> -NOTHING WILL EVER END UP AS YOU ONCE HAD IT PLANNED!<br /> -Theres two genres extremedly hard to dominate , Horror and Comedy.. if you can handle one, you can always handle the other<br /> -Dont be afraid of killing characters<br /> -Let fools die in foolish ways<br /> -Be careful with the subjects at hand, some might be more touchy than others for some players.<br /> -IF one of the players knows more science than you and he tries to Outscience you, remember..youre the ST you can fuck the game logics if you want in order to avoid him going apeshit.<br /> -Your players are the Captains of their Stories<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T20:20:00-08:00","id":398321,"title":"","content":"No plot survives contact with the players. Don't ever try to force the story you had in mind. Never say no; say &quot;yes, but...&quot; Improv is your friend. Ask your players what they want from the chronicle and what they're comfortable with, and never forget either of those lists. Fun is the number one priority. Don't try to force a game to be serious if your players aren't going for it. Never let canon get in the way of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T11:13:34-08:00","id":399046,"title":"","content":"Remember to Story-Tell much more often than you Administer Rules. <br /> <i>(As long as you are consistent, they won't even know the difference.)</i><br /> <br /> Even when people talk in game terms, they mean it in narrative terms. <br /> <i>(I got 9 dice to shoot! - really just means - My character is an amazing marksman!)</i><br /> <br /> Whenever possible, do not TELL the players, SHOW them. <br /> <i>(There is one person in the alley - means the same thing as - An old man leans against the wall, coughing into the cold air while snuffing out one smoke and lighting another.)</i><br /> <br /> When in doubt, keep the game moving along.<br /> <i>(Following ALL the rules is not as important as everyone knowing which rules are being followed.)</i><br /> <br /> Automatic successes can let you focus on the story and the important scenes. <br /> <i>(If dice pool = target difficulty, let the player choose to forgo the roll and assume one success.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}